# Frontend (`packages/client`)

- React 19 function components with named exports (`export function ChatPanel`); `App` is the default export.
- State lives in `App.tsx` and is passed down as props; components stay presentational.
- All HTTP calls go through `src/api.ts` using the relative `/api` base (Vite proxies to :3001 in
  dev, nginx proxies to `api:3001` in production).
  Errors are read from the `{ error }` body via `readError`.
- `GET /api/health` drives which LLM buttons are enabled (`llm.openai` / `llm.deepseek`).
  There is no template fallback: when neither is available the selected provider is `null`, the
  composer is disabled and the sidebar explains which key to set. Never send a chat request
  without a provider.
- Request/response and profile types live in `src/contract.ts`, together with the UI-only
  `ChatMessage`. Never redeclare an API type locally.
- Never import server Python modules – talk to the API over HTTP only.
- Show failures as an assistant chat message rather than crashing or using `alert`.
- Styles: plain CSS in `App.css` / `index.css`, no CSS framework.
- Dev server must keep `host: true` in `vite.config.ts`; inside a container `127.0.0.1` is not
  reachable from the browser. The proxy target comes from `VITE_PROXY_TARGET` (default
  `http://localhost:3001`).
- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run build` from the repo root after changes.
